userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Drawing a correct free-body diagram for stacked blocks on an incline requires isolating one body at a time, including only forces acting on that body, and recognizing that contact forces come in Newton's-third-law pairs while friction opposes the relative sliding tendency at each surface.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Each free-body diagram contains only the forces acting on the isolated body, and every contact force on one diagram has an equal-and-opposite partner on the other body's diagram.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
{
